# M10 — the production role guard's CREATEDB predicate made unmatchable.
#
# A/B partner to M9: the same drift, the same carrier role (statesman_owner, reached by
# statesman_migrator), the same shape of control. Both are CAUGHT; if one ever regresses to
# ESCAPED while the other does not, the difference is the control and not the harness.
#
# CREATEDB matters on its own because a role that can create a database owns it, and inside
# a database it owns it is free of this schema's policies and grants entirely.
id: M10
title: privileged-role's CREATEDB reason is ANDed with false, so no role ever matches it
expect: caught
proves: the production role guard's CREATEDB predicate has a control that names the reason it reported
expect-test: CREATEDB: refuses a connection that can SET ROLE to a role holding CREATEDB

file: tests/support/scoped-pg/privileged-role.ts
count: 1
@@FIND
    sql: (a) => `${a}.rolcreatedb`,
@@REPLACE
    sql: (a) => `${a}.rolcreatedb and false`,
@@END
